<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $168.1 mln April 17.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $168.1 mln April 17.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $168.1 million deficit on April 17 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 17</p>
<p>Exports: $209.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $384.8 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $165.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $157.8 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $168.1 million</p>
<p>ARPIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.695 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.891 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.740 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.239 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $305 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
